{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויעשו כן עשו", :translit "va'ya'asu ken asu", :gloss "and they did, so they did"} {:he "שתי עשיות", :translit "shtei asiyot", :gloss "two acts of making"} {:he "אחת לפסח ואחת למילה", :translit "achat la'pesach ve'achat la'milah", :gloss "one for Pesach and one for circumcision"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Doubling of the root עשה in the verse signals two distinct acts of doing"}], :frame {:text "The Israelites in Egypt needed to circumcise themselves before they could partake of the Pesach offering, as an uncircumcised person is forbidden to eat from it (Exodus 12:48). Therefore both acts were performed at the same time: every member of the household was circumcised, and then the Pesach was slaughtered and eaten.", :sources ["Exodus 12:48"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Doubling of the root עשה in the verse signals two distinct acts of doing", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:13.813699820Z", :model "glm-5.2"}